# Zuplo API Linting Example

You are working in the `api-linting` example of the Zuplo examples repository.
This example demonstrates linting a Zuplo OpenAPI config with Vacuum. It is not
run as a gateway here — the only documented workflow is `npm run lint`.

## Project Structure
- config/api-ruleset.yaml - Vacuum ruleset (the rules enforced)
- config/routes.oas.json - OpenAPI routes with x-zuplo-route extensions (the linted file)
- config/policies.json - Policy configurations
- lint-functions/*.js - Custom Vacuum lint functions
- schemas/*.json - JSON Schemas imported by the validation policies
- modules/*.ts - Custom handlers and policies
- Lint: npm run lint

## Code Conventions
- TypeScript with @zuplo/runtime imports
- Handlers: export default async function(request: ZuploRequest, context: ZuploContext)
- Policies: export default async function(request, context, options, policyName)
- Return Response objects from handlers
- Return request (continue) or Response (short-circuit) from policies

## Common Patterns
- context.log.info() for logging
- context.custom for passing data between policies
- ZoneCache for distributed caching
- environment.VAR_NAME for env vars

## When Modifying Routes
- Edit config/routes.oas.json
- Add handler reference in x-zuplo-route.handler
- Add policies in x-zuplo-route.policies.inbound/outbound
- Every policy named on a route must be defined in config/policies.json
- Every route's inbound policies must include my-auth-policy, and every path
  must start with /v1, or the lint fails

## Local Development
- npm run lint runs Vacuum over config/routes.oas.json; it must exit 0
- npx tsc --noEmit --skipLibCheck typechecks modules/
